# The Ledger — Build Workflow & Quality Standard

## Quality standard

"Does it build" is the floor, not the bar. Every change must meet:
- Correct data (no fabricated facts presented as real)
- Correct sourcing (tier values, dates, and links visible in UI)
- Correct rendering (SSR for all route pages — see below)
- No regressions (build passes, guard suites green, golden snapshots unchanged)
- Honest empty states (no fabricated fill-ins when data is missing)

## Architecture rule — SSR on all route pages

**Route pages (`app/**/page.tsx`) must be server components.** Do not add `'use client'` to a route page file. Interactive sub-components (tabs, accordions, charts) use `'use client'` — the route page itself does not.

Why: crawlers index server-rendered HTML. A `'use client'` route page is invisible to Google. The product goal is to be the best political research resource — that requires search visibility.

## Branch workflow

- **Canonical repo:** `robbieryan312-star/The-ledger` — branch **`main`** (see `REPO.md`)
- Feature branches optional for large reviews; owner may direct work on `main` when consolidating history
- **Commit locally** after each completed task when `npm run build` and all guard suites pass
- **`git push` only on Claude Code's explicit APPROVAL** — never push unreviewed phase work
- `npm run build` must pass before any commit

## Phase gates

After each phase:
1. Commit completed work locally (do not push until approved)
2. Run all guard suites + `npm run build` — report pass/fail
3. Report: what was changed, what was tested, what was NOT changed
4. Claude Code reviews against `.cursor/rules/ledger-core-rules.mdc`; on APPROVAL, push to `origin/main`
5. Owner reviews visual/product checkpoints only (marked 👁 in `PROGRESS.md`)

Report format (3 lines max):
```
Build: pass | fail
Files changed: [list]
Verified: [what you actually tested]
```

## Data change discipline

- Never launch parallel agents editing the same data files — causes regressions
- After data changes, run: `npm run sync:legislators` then `npm run verify:office`
- Build must pass: `npm run build`
- Owner runs `npm run dev` in their own terminal — do not start dev servers on port 3000

## Scope discipline

- Do not add features, refactor, or introduce abstractions beyond what the task requires
- Do not add error handling for scenarios that cannot happen
- Do not write comments that explain WHAT the code does — only WHY when non-obvious
- Scope creep (adding unrequested components, changing copy, renaming things) is a task failure

## When to stop and ask

Stop and ask Claude Code (not the owner) for credibility tradeoffs. Stop and ask the owner only for:
- Scope changes (adding features not in the brief)
- Major UX / visual / layout / product direction changes

Do not stop and ask for routine implementation decisions.

## Mock data policy (DNU quarantine — 2026-07-04)

Mock/hand-authored fact data is permanently banned from the app interface.
Historical hand-authored data was removed; retrievable only via git history (quarantine commit 288e2df).

- **Banned from interface:** No app/, components/, or lib/ code may import former DNU quarantine files
- **Guard-enforced:** Build fails on any DNU import (sourceIntegrity test suite)
- **Pipelines are the only path:** Real data enters via sync scripts → lib/data/generated/ with verifiable sources
- **Identity scaffolding:** Politician roster/identity fields live in generated/roster.json
- **Honest empty states:** Any category without real pipeline data shows "No verified record available"
- **Demo surfaces:** /elections, /lobbying, /compare show "No verified data yet" until real pipelines exist

## Sync script commands

```bash
npm run sync:legislators      # refresh congressional roster
npm run sync:fec-national     # FEC finance for all 537 members
npm run sync:votes-national   # roll-call votes (all 537 → data/national/votes/)
npm run sync:votes            # legacy per-member overlay
npm run sync:stock-trades     # STOCK Act PTR trades
npm run sync:news-rss         # approved-outlet RSS for migrated profiles
npm run verify:office         # confirm office resolution is clean
npm run build                 # must pass before any commit
```
